\nExample pathways\nPostgraduate study\nGraduate Diplomas\nPostgraduate Diploma in Science\nBachelor of Science with Honours\nMaster of Science by coursework and thesis\nMaster of Science by thesis\nMaster of Actuarial Science\nMaster of Applied Statistics\nMathematics\nStatistics\nPhD\nThesis topics and supervisors\nPostgraduate advice\nCourses offered\nAcademic course lists\nAwards and scholarships\nCareers\nInternships and work placements\nResearch\nApplied mathematics\nData science\nGeometry and analysis\nLogic and algebra\nProbability and statistics\nStatistical advice for researchers\nStudent resources\nStaff resources\nDoctor of Philosophy\nThe Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) programme involves three to four years of individually supervised research, culminating in the preparation of a thesis that is subject to external assessment and an oral examination. Students are registered provisionally for up to 12 months. Transition from provisional to full registration depends on the satisfactory completion of a written research proposal, in this School typically of up to 10 pages.\nThe Faculty of Graduate Research (FGR) provides a first contact point for all students enrolling in a PhD at Victoria University of Wellington. The Faculty website provides application forms, details of available funding, application dates and answers to frequently asked questions.\nThe FGR administers all PhD degrees across the university and all prospective PhD students should apply by the following deadlines:\n1 March\n1 July\n1 November.\nInternational students should also contact the International Office.\nProspective PhD students should contact an appropriate staff member to determine whether the topic they would like to research for their thesis can be supervised by the School. Current thesis topics and supervisors indicate areas of research interest and study.\nMore information about the PhD is on the Wellington Faculty of Science website.\nContact\nContact details for the Postgraduate Coordinators for Mathematics and for Statistics & Operations Research can be found on the Contact us page.\nUseful links\nStatistical Consultant\nUndergraduate Study\nPostgraduate Study\nCourse lists\nThesis Topics\nMore contacts\nUseful contacts\n+64 4 463 5341\ninfo@vuw.ac.nz\nEmergencies\nFaculties\nArchitecture and Design Innovation\nBusiness and Government\nEducation, Health, and Psychological Sciences\nGraduate Research\nHumanities and Social Sciences\nLaw\nScience and Engineering\nContacts and directories\nStaff directory\nMedia enquiries\nFind a researcher\nHealth and safety\nCampuses\nKelburn Campus\nPipitea Campus\nTe Aro Campus\nAuckland Premises\nStudy\nProgrammes and courses\nApply and enrol\nScholarships\nAccommodation\nSchools hub\nStudents\nLibrary\nServices and support\nFinancial survival\nKey dates\nCourses\nP\u016baha\u2014Student portal\nNuku\u2014Learning environment\nLibrary\nStaff\nStaff email\nStaff Service Centre\nMyTools for staff\nTeaching support\nWorking here\nCurrent vacancies\nAlumni\nStay connected\nGiving\nDonate\nLatest news\nEvents\nResearch expertise\nPublications\nSocial media\n0800 04 04 04\n+64 4 472 1000\ninfo@vuw.ac.nz\nEmergency: 0800 842 8888\nSite info\nSite map\nFeedback\nGlossary\nPrivacy\nCopyright \u00a9 Victoria University of Wellington, New Zealand", "links": [["", "javascript:;"], ["", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/sms/study/postgraduate-study/phd/_edit"], ["", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/"], ["Te Kura M\u0101tai Tatauranga School of Mathematics and Statistics", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/sms"], ["P\u016baha", "https://puaha.wgtn.ac.nz/"], ["Nuku", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/teaching-support/teaching-with-technology/log-in-to-nuku"], ["Staff", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/staff"], ["Apply to study", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/study/apply-enrol"], ["Apply", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/study/apply-enrol"], ["", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/"], ["Te Kahupapa Future students", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/study"], ["Te Kahupapa ki Tai International student